caption: Afterlife Capacity

Afterlife (Payload): Gods buy payload to represent the construction of afterlifes, basing their Basic Lift for this purpose on their Will, rather than lifting strength. This requires, at least, 2,000 lbs of capacity per soul, per the standard payload rules for Cabins. By default, an afterlife is basically the same as a real world, just a space for souls to exist. Most pantheons have more than one afterlife, since the features of the afterlife have to be created or purchased by the gods in question (created via magic or purchased by the god as an advantage).
